WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.300
I want you to give me special training.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.820
I-I want to get stronger...

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.660
I wanna do special training, too! Next 
time, I promise I won't be a pain!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.950
And I want our team to win next time!

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.330
Shin, me too.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:21.150
Putting together a deck, making the most of 
the units, staying a step ahead of the fight...

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.970
There's a lot that I want to study.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.880
Now these are the faces that I want to see.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.010
For kids like you...

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.110
Boom!

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.170
Team Q4's summer training camp!

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.020
Mornin'!

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.790
Morning.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.720
You're here bright and early, Kamui.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:18.180
There's still lots of time 
before we're supposed to meet.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.740
After all, the camp is so we can learn 
how to annihilate that Ren rat, right?!

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.920
When I think about that, 
I just can't stand still!

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.350
That's not entirely wrong,

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.610
but the purpose of this camp 
isn't to defeat someone.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:35.380
It's to make yourselves stronger, 
to the best of your ability.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.810
Watch out, Ren!

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.180
I'm never gonna let you 
say "It was boring" again!

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.840
It's too hot in here...

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.520
It's Summer! It's Camp! It's Vanguard!

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.900
Good morning!

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.200
Morning!

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.110
You're early too, eh, Aichi?

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.080
Huh?

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.320
Good morning!

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.590
M-Miss Emi!

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.580
You're going too, Emi?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.550
Uh-huh! I was worried about Aichi 
staying over there by himself.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.000
I told you I'm fine on my own!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.380
What are you talking about?!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.020
Who's the guy that won't get out 
of bed unless I wake him up?!

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.870
E-Emi!

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.130
Well, it's true, isn't it?!

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.120
Miss Emi gets Aichi out of bed every day...?!

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.290
Kamui, it's morning! Wake up!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.890
I wanna sleep some more...

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:40.500
Kamui, you'd sleep all day if you could!

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.030
I...

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.490
I'm so jealous of you, Brother!

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:51.210
What, Kamui?

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.350
Never mind...

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.890
You did talk to your mother 
about it, I presume?

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:57.720
Yes!

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.910
Then there's no problem.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.780
Let's go together, Emi!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.330
Yay!

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.900
Together with Miss Emi...

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.990
That means...

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.070
Wait for me!

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.340
This way!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.000
Emi!

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.600
Come on, wait up, I said!

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.330
Yo! Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:33.900
Hey, peeps!

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.640
What are you two here for?

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.700
The training camp, of course!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.530
Do you understand the 
meaning of "training camp"?

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:42.230
Naturally!

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:46.980
Card training camp can't start without 
Card Capital's strongest fighter,

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.410
the great Katsumi Morikawa, right?

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.460
You're obviously not dressed to play cards.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.830
Quit picking on us!

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.070
Besides, the more the merrier, right?

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:01.710
Words of wisdom. That's right.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.890
There's plenty of room, so you 
guys are more than welcome!

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:06.950
Yes!!

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:08.740
Well, of course.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.120
I'll train everyone!

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:10.930
Right...

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.800
What's wrong, Aichi?

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.440
Nothing...

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.160
You're worried about Kai, aren't you?

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.670
Y-Yeah...

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.410
You shouldn't give that guy a second thought!

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:24.310
He doesn't come to events like this, does he?

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.390
I don't think he's into group activities...

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:28.320
But...

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.880
It's okay. Miwa is sure to bring him over.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:34.080
Miwa?

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.380
Yes. And I've prepared bait, too.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.220
Bait?

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.150
What's up, everyone?

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.530
I see the gang's all here.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.790
Let go of me! I'm not gonna run away.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.360
Kai!

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.660
I was positive he wouldn't show up!

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.570
Is what you told me really true?

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.730
We'll see...

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:54.540
Why, you...

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.120
This is all of us.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.000
Um...

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.410
1-2-3-4-5...

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.440
6-7-8...

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.180
A total of eight, huh?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.890
Count yourself, too!

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.280
I-I did that on purpose!

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.520
But either way, we can't all fit into 
the manager's beat-up old van...

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.110
Sorry, but...

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.920
What?! I'm definitely going!

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.830
I'm absolutely going!

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.840
I'm going to the beach!

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:26.640
There's no need to worry.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:32.620
See? I've prepared the perfect vehicle.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.170
You had me going for a moment there...

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.520
Wait, you knew and were 
just yanking my chain?!

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:40.730
Could be...

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.950
She was totally toying with him...

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:50.890
She may not look it, but even Misaki's 
spirits are raised by summer camp.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:55.930
It's hard to tell...

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.620
Everyone's in, right?!

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.410
Are your seat belts fastened?!

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.770
We're just waiting on you.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.760
Then, everyone in unison...

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:11.570
Here we go!

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:12.610
Shut up!

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:24.700
The sea!

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.910
The mountains!

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:28.980
Vacation!

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.730
It's <i>training camp</i>.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.070
Wow...

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.520
The fragrance of the tides!

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.810
Nothing says summer better than the beach!

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:45.060
This would be a perfect picture...

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:49.430
Well? Once in a while, this 
kind of thing is nice, right?

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.320
Izaki! Aichi! Let's go for a swim first!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.970
Wait a minute!

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.780
Oh, that's right.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:00.710
Need to warm up before swimming...

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.760
1-2-3-4...

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.050
No, not that.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:07.060
We're staying at that cottage today,

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.330
so please carry the luggage there.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.590
Let's do that later!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.210
No, sir.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:18.650
It's better to get nuisances out of the 
way first, just like with homework.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:22.200
Which reminds me, how is everyone's 
summer vacation homework progressing?

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.660
Don't remind me of unpleasantries...

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:28.150
Mine's going according to plan!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.010
Of course.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.780
Manager, you're just like our teacher!

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.850
Well, let's get to it.

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:42.940
W-What is all this luggage?!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.190
It looks like a big job. Want some help?

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.080
That'd be great...

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.040
Have I seen you people before somewhere...?

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.210
Team Caesar!

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.300
Manager, what is this?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:02.240
They're actually the ones who 
invited us to this training camp.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.760
It may be rude to put it like this,

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.760
but you guys showed promise.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:12.130
Despite not making it past 
the elimination round,

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:16.040
you snatched one match away 
from AL4 through ability alone,

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:20.120
a feat that Team Quadrifoglio 
only shares with our team.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:24.930
To be honest, I wanted this training 
camp to also be our celebration,

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.900
but, unfortunately, it 
didn't work out that way.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:33.030
But thanks to that, we now have 
the same aim, to defeat AL4.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.300
Defeat AL4...

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.550
Sounds good to me! I'm all fired up!

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:42.230
Well? This is the optimum combination 
for a training camp, don't you think?

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:46.160
They're ahead of Q4 when it 
comes to total power as a team,

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.000
so I think you can learn a lot.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:49.800
Yep!

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:54.440
You act carefree, but the wheels 
are always turning, huh, Shin?

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:55.420
Surprisingly...

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.490
"Surprisingly" was uncalled for.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.120
And call me "Manager", all right?

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:05.170
I was looking forward to meeting you.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.890
Me too.

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:11.550
Huh? Kai, you knew that 
they were going to be here?

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.210
Yeah. That's why I came.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:18.450
I see. So <i>they're</i> the bait 
that Manager mentioned.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:19.620
Right.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:23.810
At nationals, he didn't get the chance 
to face off against Team Caesar,

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.060
so I told him he'd be 
able to fight them here.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.200
I get it...

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.000
You will fight?

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.570
You know it.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.520
Toshiki Kai and Kenji Mitsusada...

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.470
This fight'll be one for the ages!

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:36.040
Pfft...

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:39.810
It's a match-up that wouldn't be out 
of place at the national finals.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.800
I can't wait!

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:45.030
If you're going to fight, 
we've got the perfect place.

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:46.960
I'll lead the way, so follow me.

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:55.710
Miss Emi, let's go too.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:56.440
Sure!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:03.060
Hey, everyone! What about the sea?!

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.410
I'm coming back for sure later!

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.420
Wait for me, ocean!

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:16.830
Um, has everyone forgotten about the luggage?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.430
What should I do with all this?

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.090
All the way up there...

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.550
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.000
Stand up the Vanguard!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.530
It's boring just watching, isn't it?

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:39.660
Look!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.810
Let's do it, too.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:46.490
Sure!

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.960
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:06.070
I lose.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:10.980
Seriously?! The leader 
of Team Kaiser, beaten?!

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:12.460
That's what you might expect from Kai.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:16.180
Looks like Team Caesar is no big deal...

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:17.710
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.450
I figured he'd say that.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:24.280
In the 7th turn, maybe I should have 
intercepted instead of guarding from my hand.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.820
You knew what was in my hand 
because of the trigger, right?

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.960
Yeah. It didn't help narrow 
down any intelligence.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:32.080
Your only problem was 
maintaining the front line.

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:33.670
I see...

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:36.590
When I think about the cards 
that were left in my deck,

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:41.580
I had an 80% chance or better of getting 
the power that I needed on my next draw.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.780
You forgot that your opponent 
was using a Kagero deck.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:46.010
I get it.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:49.500
If I had considered the risk of 
being driven off with a skill...

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:51.050
Whew...

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:53.370
I have no idea what they're talking about...

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.650
They're just flapping their gums!

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:58.680
A real man is quiet and uses grade 3 units!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.240
Strongest

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:00.270
That's how the fight is won!

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:03.310
Yeah... Yeah, right, but...

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:04.750
You got it rough...

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:07.000
How's Aichi doing?

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:10.490
It's my turn.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:16.110
I attack Gordon with Masked Police, Grander!

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.270
I activate Grander's skill.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:22.450
Super Dimensional Robo, Daiyusha's 
power is increased by +2000!

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.370
I guard with Gallatin!

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:29.840
Next, I use this Grander...

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.520
to attack Gordon with a 
boost from Karenroid, Daisy!

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:38.140
With Grander's skill, Daiyusha's 
power increases by another +2000!

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:40.330
No guard.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.450
With a boost from Daisy,

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:45.760
Daiyusha attacks Gancelot!

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.250
Daiyusha's power exceeds 14000,

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:50.520
so I can activate its skill!

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:59.280
During battle, Daiyusha's 
critical is given +1!

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:03.380
With 2 more damage, I'll lose,

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:08.310
but with Daisy's boost, the 
total attack is 22000...

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:10.620
Gancelot's power is 9000.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:14.040
Even if I guard with Epona, that 
only brings it up to 19000...

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.090
I can't block it...

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.390
No guard.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:20.950
Twin drive, first check...

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:24.990
Second check...

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.980
Army Penguin. Draw trigger.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.530
I give Daiyusha +5000!

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.570
I draw...

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.980
I attack Gancelot!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.800
Damage trigger check!

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.750
One more card...

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:45.970
No trigger.

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:50.340
Awww, he lost.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:56.610
What do you think? Wanna 
try and redeem yourself?

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.140
Y-Yes!

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.780
How many more trips...?

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:08.670
Again?!

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:14.210
That makes five losses in a row. That's 
losing way too many times, and no mistake.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:15.310
Sorry.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.880
But there was nothing 
wrong with your playing.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:22.020
Can I see your deck for a minute?

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.070
Sure.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:31.550
How is it?

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:33.750
Not bad.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:34.750
The only thing...

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:36.160
The only thing?

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:39.430
Well, when you come right down to it,

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:42.660
in terms of a winning image, 
it's kind of a lean deck.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:44.750
Winning... image?

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:46.660
Sendou...

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:50.660
Do you have a clear image 
of how you're going to

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.380
win with this deck?

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.800
Um... That, uh...

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:57.720
How I'm going to win...

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:00.780
If you can clearly imagine that,

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:04.500
you should be able to naturally understand 
which cards are necessary and which aren't.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:05.940
Oh...

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:11.450
All right! Next, the strongest fighter here, 
the great Katsumi Morikawa, will play!

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.200
So! Who's cruisin' for a bruisin'?!

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:16.820
Okay, I'll play you.

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:21.610
Fine! But don't be surprised by the 
great Morikawa's maximum-strength deck!

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:22.430
I can't wait...

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.960
Imagine how I'm going to win...

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:34.820
I-I think that's about enough for today!

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.010
About enough?

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.830
That was your 13th loss in a row!

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.030
O-Oh, shut up!

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:42.280
What does my horoscope 
say about my luck today?

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:46.260
Um, "Your luck is on the skids, with 
cloudy skies turning to a downpour."

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:49.210
Isn't that what you said 
yesterday and the day before?

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.760
But that's what it really says!

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.850
Look! A "downpour"! "Rain"! 
"Typhoon"! "Lightning"!

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:59.450
Well, let's put the cards away for a while.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:01.480
We're finally going to the beach, huh?!

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:02.380
No.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:09.410
You're all going to make dinner.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.550
We're going to make it?

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.780
Dinner made by team effort is delicious!

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:18.380
I've never cooked before.

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:20.440
But I'm sure I can do it if I try!

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:21.820
I don't wanna eat that...

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:27.240
Don't say that! Come on, you can think that 
I tricked you all the while you're making it.

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:36.750
Jeepers! Be careful not 
to hurt yourself, Aichi!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:39.630
Yeah. It slipped a little...

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:42.930
Peeling potatoes is hard, isn't it?

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:44.640
It's simple!

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:47.470
You just can't do it because 
you never help out.

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:54.050
I don't know why, but I'm crying like a baby!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.340
Me too!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:58.490
For some reason, the tears won't stop!

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.970
It's because you're chopping onions...

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:03.020
Come to think of it, where's Kai?

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:05.860
Did you call me?

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:07.990
N-No...

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:10.090
I see. Fine, then.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:14.530
I guess he's got an unexpected talent...

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.200
But you don't need to mince 
vegetables for curry!

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:22.380
Fried light brown onions give 
the roux a well-seasoned flavor.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:26.120
E-Excuse the interruption...

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.950
Aren't they light brown enough?

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.690
Not yet.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:40.460
Okay, I'm going to open it.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:46.600
Thanks for the food!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.090
Well? Delicious, isn't it?

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.340
Yes!

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:58.980
It's different than Mom's curry, but 
it's still really good, right, Aichi?

00:18:58.980 --> 00:18:59.900
Uh huh!

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:02.720
I wouldn't expect anything less 
from curry that Miss Emi made!

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:04.500
It's scrumptious!

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:06.350
It could be worse...

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:09.110
Seconds!

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.400
Get it yourself.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:17.290
A time like this does call for curry...

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:18.890
Everyone's got a smiling face.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.210
The dishes are done.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.790
And we had plenty of fights...

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:27.250
Dinner's finished...

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:29.370
We had watermelon for dessert...

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.500
All right! <i>Now</i> it's time for the beach!

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:32.740
What are you talking about?

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:34.350
It's pitch black.

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:35.530
What?!

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:38.230
Shoot!

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:42.650
Don't be so down in the dumps! 
There's still tomorrow.

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:45.870
Besides, there's something else 
that's fun to do at night.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.370
Aichi, you're getting too rattled!

00:19:58.370 --> 00:20:01.280
Really?! Those aren't fireworks you 
do at night! Are you a little kid?!

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:04.460
Don't scare me!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.620
And those are my fireworks!

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:11.250
I was looking forward to 
lighting that 100-shooter!

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.500
Kinda underwhelming...

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.020
You're right...

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:30.750
That was a nice, hot 
bath, wasn't it, Brother?

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.720
Yep!

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:34.660
Aichi, did you do a good 
job washing your hair, too?

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.590
Y-Yeah, I washed it.

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.140
Really?

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:40.230
Relax, Miss Emi.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:42.210
I made sure.

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:43.850
He even used conditioner!

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:46.000
No problem then.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.290
Aichi! Let's have a pillow fight!

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.960
No, sir. Tomorrow's an early day.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:58.320
And if you oversleep, you 
won't have time to swim.

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:59.720
I-I see...

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:02.410
Hurry up and turn off the light, Aichi!

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:06.390
But don't make it pitch black! 
Keep a little light on!

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:09.120
There's no end to that loudmouth!

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:39.500
Nagisa! Stop it, Nagisa!

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:47.030
Image of how I'm going to win...

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.370
You'll strain your eyes.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:51.580
Manager...

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:54.240
I hope you'll get something 
out of this training camp.

00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:55.910
Yeah.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:07.160
Maybe I need to give you 
a little more help...

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:13.180
At any rate, we'll continue tomorrow.

00:23:51.620 --> 00:23:53.430
It's great going through training 
camp with everyone, you know?

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:54.710
Of course!

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:57.610
Making curry, lighting fireworks, 
having a pillow fight before bed...

00:23:58.150 --> 00:23:59.600
That's different from training camp!

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:01.700
Oh, I see! I forgot!

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:03.990
The beach! Swimming! Swimsuits!

00:24:03.990 --> 00:24:06.050
Next time: Results of the Training Camp!

00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:10.720
Hey, Morikawa, I tried reassembling my deck 
according to the image in my head, but...

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:12.470
Huh? Morikawa?

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:15.070
It looks like he exhausted himself from 
being overexcited and snoozed right off.

00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:17.030
I'm swimming tomorrow...
